{ This study is about openings that start with the f-pawn. A bird flies the furthest. With this hint, open with the Bird opening! }
1. f4 { For white, this opening is called the Bird or the Dutch Attack. If you do not want to progress with your f-pawn to the max, try the Barnes Opening! } (1. f3 { This is the Barnes Opening. You can progress further with your f-pawn though. }) 1... f5 { For black this is called the Dutch defense, As a response to the Bird opening we get The Symmetrical Variation. Copycat is a good defence against the Birdopening if white plays at his best and black is not familiair with the Bird. } 2. g3 g6 3. d3 d6 4. e4 e5 5. Nf3 Nf6 6. Nc3 Nc6 7. Bg2 Bg7 8. exf5 exf4 9. fxg6 fxg3 10. Qe2+ Qe7 11. Qxe7+ { No the copycat strategy is over but white has only gained a slight advance to black. } 11... Nxe7 { But because the Bird is not a common opening, white has the extra advantage of being more familiar with this position. } *


