1. e4 { [%clk 0:05:00] } 1... f5 { [%clk 0:05:00] } 2. Qh5+ { [%clk 0:04:58] } 2... g6 { This is the strongest move! But be aware for Be2 } { [%clk 0:04:59] } 3. Be2 { Not a strong move by white. Unless..... } { [%clk 0:04:57] } 3... e5 { Wise choice. You were not tempted to take the poisonous Queen. } (3... gxh5 { You're checkmated after Bh5. The most dangerous h-diagonal in the F-pawn openings, } { [%csl Re8][%cal Ge2h5] [%clk 0:04:57] } 4. Bxh5# { 1-0 White wins by checkmate. } { [%clk 0:04:57] }) 4. Qf3 Nc6 5. exf5 { Now it is clear why we previous did Nc6 } 5... Nd4 { Now the fast Queen walks into the trap itself. } 6. Qd3 d5 7. fxg6 Bf5 8. Bh5 Kd7 9. Qg3 Nxc2+ 10. Kd1 hxg6 11. Bxg6 Qf6 12. Bxf5+ Qxf5 13. Qf3 Qg6 14. Qxd5+ Bd6 15. d3 Nxa1 *


