1. f4 e5 { Again the From gambit. Let's now transpose this in the King's gambit. } 2. e4 exf4 { The Gambit is accepted. } 3. Nf3 g5 { Allow black to drive away your knight with his pawn in order to set a trap. } { [%cal Gg5g4] } 4. Nc3 { The importance of this move is to protect the pawn, so the black Queen can not capture it. } { [%cal Gc3e4,Rd8h4] } 4... g4 5. Ne5 { [%cal Ge5f7,Ge5g4] } 5... Qh4+ { [%csl Ge1][%cal Re1e2] } 6. g3 fxg3 7. Qxg4 { If black changes Queen's white's development is ahead in exchange for a pawn. } { [%csl Gh4][%cal Rh4g4,Gh4f2] } 7... g2+ 8. Qxh4 gxh1=Q 9. Qh5 { If black defends the pawn on f7 white can attack the defender by the d4. move } { [%cal Rg8h6,Gd2d4,Bc1h6] } 9... Be7 10. Nxf7 Nf6 11. Nd6+ Kd8 12. Qe8+ Rxe8 13. Nf7# *


