{ Let's play a scenario where again white accepts the gambit. You can learn about this line on https://lichess.org/study/WDUOUjVe/VbCCgBtl. }
1. e4 f5 2. exf5 { This is the Duras gambit accepted by white. This is best reaction for white and by far the most common. } 2... Nf6 { The best move for white is d4. } { [%cal Gd2d4] } 3. Qf3 Nc6 4. Nc3 Nd4 { This moves uses the fact that the Queen is exposed and forces it to retreat after which you can recapture the pawn. Black has gained in development and removed the King's pawn. However this is not the best move according to stockfish. For beginner's however this line seems to be the most playable for black. } { [%csl Gf3][%cal Gf3d1,Gd4f5,Rf3g4,Rf3h5,Rf3e2,Rf3e4,Gd4c2,Rf3f4,Gf3d3] } (4... d5 { The best move for white but complicated to play for a beginner, Try a simpler one! }) (4... e5 { The second best move. Reserve it for later! }) 5. Qd3 e5 6. fxe6 Nxe6 { Here the gambit gives black a little advantage in development in exchange for a pawn. which is equalizing according to stockfish. } *


