{ Open with the Bird! }
1. f4 Nc6 { Black reacts to the Bird opening by bringing his knight to Nc3. The best reaction for White is also the recommended move if Black had reacted with d5 (dutch variation), e6 or Nh3 (horsefly). } { [%cal Bd7d5,Be7e6,Bg8h6] } 2. Nf3 { This is why we call this chapter the Bird knight. We already saw that the knights on the g-file play an important role in f-pawn openings. } 2... d6 3. e4 e5 { A lot of good moves are possible for white. Find the strongest one! } 4. d4 { Very suprising and good move. This opens up many possibilities for white to make it an interesting game. There is no real threat anymore by Qh4. } { [%cal Gc6d4,Ge5d4,Gf3d4,Gd1d4,Rd8h4,Rg2g3,Be5f4,Bc1f4] } (4. fxe5 { Fine move. Try a stronger one }) (4. Bb5 { Fine move. Try a stronger one. }) (4. Nc3 { Fine move. Try a stronger one! }) (4. d3 { Good move. Try a stronger one, }) 4... Nxd4 5. Nxd4 exd4 6. Qxd4 *


