{ Again let's play the Dutch variation of the Bird opening. }
1. f4 d5 2. Nf3 Bg4 3. e3 { Prevent indeed black from destroying your pawn structure. The pin on the Queen is for now not dangerous because the white knight is not attacked nor is it defending anything. Learn more about the Dutch Variation on https://lichess.org/study/UgA8sHAU. } (3. Nc3 { You allow black to destroy your lawn structure on the king side. } { [%cal Gg4f3,Ge2f3] }) (3. Ne5 { Interesting agressive respons. Forcing the black bishop to retreat. Threatening to destroy black pawn structure instead. Try a more defending approach. } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gg4f5,Gc2c4,Gf7f6,Ge5f3] }) 3... Bxf3 { This is the most common response on the LiChess database but not a good one according to Stockfish and chessmasters. } 4. Qxf3 e6 5. Be2 Nf6 *


