{ Open with the Bird }
1. f4 c5 2. e4 { This is the McDonnell Attack which in most cases arises when playing the Sicilian Defense 1.e4 c5. White should take the opportunity to occupy the centre like with any pawn move on the which allows this! } { [%cal Ge2e4,Bf2f4,Gc7c5,Ga7a6,Ga7a5,Gb7b6,Gb7b5,Gc7c6,Gd7d6,Ge7e6,Gg7g6,Gf7f6,Gh7h6,Gh7h5] } (2. Nf3 { take the opportunity to occupy the centre! }) 2... Qc7 { This is a very uncommon reaction to the attack. } 3. d4 { This is the best move (stockfish level 37). You can drill more common McDonnell Attack variations on https://lichess.org/study/NfjNlFdo } (3. d3 { This is a logical and ok reaction to the Queen attacking the f4 pawn. But and even more agressive move works even better. }) 3... cxd4 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. Nxd4 a6 6. Be2 e6 7. Nc3 Nxd4 8. Qxd4 *


